From 83f05fe66ac6738f9a573fb0867d47cb4ff26df1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 18:01:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Menu: a left column, boxed-less rows with a pointing hand,
 descriptions on the right, menu sounds

The in-game menu becomes a column down the left edge with the game showing to its right through a fading scrim: a blue section band instead of
the tab strip, rows underlined in blue (the focused one darker, with the game's pointing hand, which moves in a quick beep-beep), the focused
row's description as plain white text on the right, and the confirmation windows in that space too. A drag on the right scrolls the list on a
touch screen. The scrollbar is a thin gradient. The text is smaller on a computer (2.6% of the window height; a phone keeps 3.4%).
The hand is read from the texture pack (ui/handsmall.png), a triangle without it.

The menu has sounds (ui/ui_sound.cpp): a click when the cursor or the section changes, a back sound when a screen is left or the menu
closes, one for a switch on and one off, one for Quit game. They are WAV files in <data>/sounds (navigate, back, confirm, toggle_on,
toggle_off); the port ships none. The Audio tab has a "Menu sounds" switch (audio.menu_sounds).
